Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["MultiwayLongestDerivation", "ObjectName",
 CellID->611683540,ExpressionUUID->"8ce93db3-72d3-2f4a-9006-f0d1464c0077"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"062e05bd-757f-cb49-b0f9-467a6f1fbe9e"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["MultiwayLongestDerivation",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
MultiwayLongestDerivation"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "evolution", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2bdb2e70-56e3-cb43-a393-6aba4b3e1f3f"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the length of the longest derivation from the initial state of the \
[CanonicalMultiwayEvolution](paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/\
ref/CanonicalMultiwayEvolution) result ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["evolution", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0e8259f1-ce72-0149-804c-22c238b5082a"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["MultiwayLongestDerivation",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/\
MultiwayLongestDerivation"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", "limits"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8c0ff926-0fd7-334f-92d3-490477a69cea"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "evolves first.",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
  "d75559bc-b6e9-d949-aec0-3b5c9db4a28f"]
}], "Usage",
 CellID->308126451,ExpressionUUID->"4b2d357d-4cc6-a140-86ad-5b0323e6c3f9"],

Cell["\<\
The value is exact when the evolution halted. For a capped acyclic \
exploration it is the longest derivation found within the limits. When a \
cycle makes derivations unbounded the result is \
Missing[\"CyclicStatesGraph\"].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->608871045,ExpressionUUID->"25fd29ee-d0f5-634e-b564-8e9a15a0e990"],

Cell["\<\
This is the lifetime objective of the default goal. The diagnostic \
MultiwayLifetime is the breadth-first discovery depth, which can be smaller: \
a state first reached early can also lie at the end of a longer derivation.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->643404823,ExpressionUUID->"decc26a1-31e5-c941-a04c-567ac0a57208"],

Cell["\<\
In a formal model of this breadth-first canonical explorer, machine-checked \
in Lean 4 with Mathlib, a \"Halted\" status implies that every derivation \
from the initial state is finite and shorter than the number of explored \
states, and the longest derivation equals the longest path of the explored \
graph. This holds for a complete, invariant canonical form (the default \
\"Exact\" backend) and also when canonical forms are merely isomorphic copies \
(the \"Native\" backend). That this code implements the model is tested, not \
machine-checked.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->778455447,ExpressionUUID->"8c5f957c-c0d7-124d-b3b4-148f141ffe97"]
}, Open  ]],

